  "id": "finger-flexion-grip",
  "name": "Dynamic Crush Grip",
  "definition": "A local open-chain isolation whose training-defining phase repeatedly closes the fingers against a purpose-built grip trainer. This is not a generic grip family. The initial record owns only Osawa's three-by-thirty repeated-grip task with one 30 kg-rated trainer, represented one unilateral set at a time as a catalog adaptation. The rating is an implement resistance label rather than lifted mass, so the exercise is non-comparable and contributes no tonnage or load PR. The source did not report the trainer's handle or spring geometry, closure endpoint, cadence, wrist, forearm, elbow, or body posture; the contract preserves those limitations instead of inventing a standardized technique. Static support remains inside carries and implement-owning lifts; dynamometer squeezes remain assessments; pinch awaits thumb and intrinsic-hand anatomy; hangs belong to a closed-chain shoulder-body review; and wrist rollers remain multi-action conditioning.",
